    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 9: Closer look at comparison of algorithms in Safety Gym CarGoal and PointButton Environments.",
      "bbox": [
        114.75800323486328,
        394.5047912597656,
        497.2467041015625,
        402.520751953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RESPO: In the CarGoal Environment, our approach achieves the best performance among the safe",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        417.5408020019531,
        504.00079345703125,
        426.5669250488281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RL algorithms while being within the acceptable range of cost violations. It is important to note",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        428.5693664550781,
        503.9973449707031,
        437.4759216308594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "that our algorithm has no access to information on the cost threshold. In PointButton, RESPO",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        439.3587951660156,
        504.0006103515625,
        448.3849182128906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "achieves very high reward performance among the safety baselines while maintaining among the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        450.3873596191406,
        503.997314453125,
        459.2939147949219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lowest violations.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        461.2963562011719,
        178.0470428466797,
        470.2029113769531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PPOLag: In both Safety Gym environments, PPOLag maintains relatively high performance, albeit",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        477.5657958984375,
        504.0036926269531,
        486.5919189453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "less than our approach. Nonetheless, it always converges to the cost threshold amount of violations",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        488.5943603515625,
        504.00103759765625,
        497.50091552734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for the respective environments.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        499.50335693359375,
        235.5810546875,
        508.409912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "RCRL: RCRL has either high reward and high violations or low reward and low violations. It learns",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        515.7717895507812,
        504.00335693359375,
        524.7979125976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a very conservative behavior in CarGoal environment where the violations go down but the reward",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        526.8003540039062,
        503.9989013671875,
        535.7069091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "performance can also be seen to be sacrificed during training. For PointButton, RCRL achieves",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        537.5907592773438,
        504.0019836425781,
        546.6168823242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "slightly higher reward performance but has over 3× the number of violations as RESPO.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        547.902099609375,
        463.5416564941406,
        557.5259399414062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "FAC: Using a NN to represent the lagrange multiplier in order to capture the feasible sets seems to",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        564.8877563476562,
        504.0017395019531,
        573.9138793945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "produce very conservative behavior that sacrifices performance. In both CarGoal and PointButton",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        575.9163818359375,
        503.9951477050781,
        584.8229370117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the reward performance and cost violations are very low. This can be explained because the average",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        586.8253784179688,
        503.99603271484375,
        595.73193359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "observed lagrange multiplier across the states quickly grows, even becoming 9× that of scalar",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        597.01708984375,
        504.1739807128906,
        606.6409301757812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "learnable lagrange multiplier in RESPO.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        608.5247802734375,
        271.53466796875,
        617.5509033203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CBF: The CBF approach has low reward performance in both the Safety Gym benchmarks and its",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        624.9127807617188,
        503.99981689453125,
        633.9389038085938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "cost violations are quite high.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        635.9413452148438,
        225.6084747314453,
        644.847900390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CRPO, P3O, & PCPO: These CMDP-based primal approaches have mediocre reward performance",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        652.2108154296875,
        503.9972839355469,
        661.2369384765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "but, with the exception of CRPO, achieve violations within the cost threshold. CRPO, however, has",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        663.2393798828125,
        504.00323486328125,
        672.1459350585938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "high cost violations in both CarGoal and PointButton.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        674.1483764648438,
        322.763671875,
        683.054931640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanilla PPO: This unconstrained algorithm consistently has high rewards and high costs, so maxi-",
